# NOTE: the three *.i3d.terrain.*.cache files are deliberately NOT ignored.
# They used to be, on the theory that the engine regenerates them on load.
# It does -- but for this 4096 terrain that regeneration is ~71MB of derived
# data and took 10-15 minutes per load on an Apple M3 Pro (measured 2026-09-01:
# the stall began within 40ms of the "Missing terrain occluder cache" warning
# in every run). GIANTS ships all three caches with every base map for exactly
# this reason. They are tracked via LFS (see .gitattributes) and shipped in
# the release zip. GE rewrites them on save whenever the terrain changes.

# Manual backup copies made during editing (git history is the real backup)
*_backup.*

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Python build junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Traffic pipeline staging output — regenerated from map/CSVdata3 by
# tools/traffic/*.py, already merged into map/map.i3d. Not source, not shipped.
tools/traffic/manvel_traffic_import.i3d
tools/traffic/csvsplines_terrain_snap.i3d
tools/traffic/parked_cars.i3d
AutoDrive*.xml

# Release build output (tools/build_release.py)
/releases/

# Regenerable dev-tool preview images (see each tool's README for the
# one-line command to rebuild). Not runtime assets, not worth tracking.
tools/pda/pda_output.png
tools/soilMap/soilMap_preview.png
